# Review is required, and by whom, as an enforced property of the repository
# rather than a convention.
#
# The default owner covers everything. The paths below are called out so that a
# change to one of them is visibly a security or contract review rather than an
# ordinary one — the reviewer should know, from the file list alone, that they
# are looking at credential handling, at what gets sent to the API, or at what
# ships to npm.

* @Chippers255

# Credential handling. config.ts decides where the API key is stored and with
# what permissions; api-client.ts decides what leaves the machine and in which
# header.
/src/lib/config.ts        @Chippers255
/src/lib/api-client.ts    @Chippers255

# The error and exit-code contract. Agents branch on these values.
/src/lib/errors.ts        @Chippers255
/src/lib/run-action.ts    @Chippers255

# The pipeline, the task runner, and the scanners' configuration.
/.github/                 @Chippers255
/Makefile                 @Chippers255
/scripts/                 @Chippers255
/.gitleaks.toml           @Chippers255

# What ships to npm. `files`, `bin` and `engines` decide what users install.
/package.json             @Chippers255
/tsup.config.ts           @Chippers255
